        "side": "new",
        "severity": "high",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "MOV r/m64, imm32 now uses 4-byte width; loses sign-extension and 8-byte write",
        "explanation": "Mov_rm64_imm32 (REX.W C7 /0) must sign-extend imm32 to 64 bits and write 8 bytes. The old u32tou64 variant did that. With mov_rm_imm!(u32), both get_op and set_op use size 4, so a memory destination gets only 4 bytes written (upper 4 bytes of the target left stale). A register destination may also be zero-extended instead of sign-extended, for example with a negative immediate.",
        "suggestion": "Read the immediate as 4 bytes, sign-extend it to u64 (as i32 as i64 as u64), and call set_op with size 8. Or add a dedicated macro for this instruction.",
        "evidence": "    mov_rm_imm!(u32);",
        "confidence": 0.7,
        "id": "8b28e54c5105",
